{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa's Stories"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Apartment Hunting"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe rooms, homes and objects in buildings in common social and work situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Have Got"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use have <span class=\"italic\">got + infinitive</span> to talk about obligation (something you must do) or talk about an arrangement for the future that is already made."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have got to call this number. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have got to book a tour of the apartment.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We have got to clean the apartment for the next tenant."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Comparatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you compare two things you use a <span class =\"strong\">comparative</span>.  You can use <span class=\"italic\">as \u2026 as</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We can show that two things are equal using <span class =\"strong\">as + adjective + as</span></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are no differences between the two compared things. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> This apartment is as nice as the other one.<br /> This red couch is as big as the black couch.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">When we use this structure, the first thing mentioned is 'less' than the second thing. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> This place is not as cheap as the other apartment.</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bedroom "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a room for sleeping in "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a one-bedroom condo."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear when talking about an apartment. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "living room "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the main room in a house where people relax "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The living room has a large television. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to furnish "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to provide things in a room "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is the living room furnished?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "refrigerator "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large piece of kitchen equipment you use to  keep food cool "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The kitchen includes a refrigerator. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "washer and dryer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a washing machine and a clothes dryer "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I have to buy a washer and dryer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "square foot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a unit of area equal to one foot by one foot  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The condo is 1,500 square feet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rent "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the money you pay to use a place that belongs to someone else "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How much is the rent?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "steep"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "high; expensive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's a little steep for me.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lease"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an agreement that allows you to use a building for a period of time, in return for rent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do I have to sign a lease?   "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tenant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who lives in an apartment and pays rent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have got to clean the apartment for the next tenant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose two objects in your classroom."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare them. What is the same about both of them? What is different about them?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short paragraph (6-7 sentences) about them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">as ... as</span> and <span class=\"italic\">not as ... as</span> in your paragraph. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your paragraph. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraph to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to their paragraph. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about objects in a room."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare things using <span class=\"italic\">as ... as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">not as ... as</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my paragraph aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen to my partner's paragraph."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le03ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le03ob09re2img06.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le03ob09re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I have got to call this number. Hi. I'm calling about your listing.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Apartment Manage</span>r: What'd you like to know?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: How big is it?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Apartment Manager</span>: It's a one-bedroom. It's as big as other one bedrooms. There's a living room, dining room, the usual. It's furnished with a refrigerator, washer and dryer, stove, and oven.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le03ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Okay. How much square feet is it? What about the rent?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Apartment Manager</span>: 1,500 square feet for $1500 a month.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That's a little steep. I found an apartment not as expensive as this one a few blocks down. It was bigger too. Do I have to sign a lease?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Apartment Manager</span>: Yes, you can cancel the agreement during that period but you lose your deposit.", "id": 2, "time": "21000", "image": "engenn5le03ob09re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"stron